<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://kyunnilee.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://kyunnilee.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-11-23T22:26:14+00:00</updated><id>https://kyunnilee.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>Anne&apos;s personal website </subtitle><entry><title type="html">APRO: Measuring Agentic Physical Reasoning</title><link href="https://kyunnilee.github.io/blog/2026/apro/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="APRO: Measuring Agentic Physical Reasoning"/><published>2026-11-23T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-11-23T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://kyunnilee.github.io/blog/2026/apro</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://kyunnilee.github.io/blog/2026/apro/"><![CDATA[ <div class="tldr"> <b>TL;DR</b> <p>We build <b>APRO</b>, a simulator benchmark that tests whether VLMs can <b>use physical reasoning to act</b>, not just answer questions about physics.</p> <p>480 items, 11 tasks, 3 regimes: <b>infer</b> properties, <b>predict</b> from past trials, and <b>adapt</b> through interaction.</p> <p>Models get better with evidence, but <b>turning that into successful robot actions is still hard</b>.</p> <p><a href="#">Paper</a> · <a href="#">Code</a> · <a href="#">Dataset</a></p> </div> <figure> <img src="/assets/img/blog/apro/fig1_regimes.png" alt="Three evaluation regimes of APRO"/> <figcaption><b>Figure 1:</b> APRO evaluates VLMs in three nested regimes.</figcaption> </figure> <h2 id="motivation">Motivation</h2> <p>A robot picks up a hammer and it tilts. That tilt tells it where the mass is, so it should grasp somewhere else before swinging.</p> <p>Existing benchmarks test either <strong>physics understanding</strong> (fixed images, no action) or <strong>task success</strong> (no view into why it failed). We want both, in one loop.</p> <figure> <div class="vgrid"> <div class="cell"> <video src="/assets/video/blog/apro/hammer_franka_argon.mp4" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline=""></video> <span class="tag-ok">Success</span> · Gemini 4 Argon </div> <div class="cell"> <video src="/assets/video/blog/apro/hammer_franka_sol.mp4" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline=""></video> <span class="tag-fail">Fail</span> · GPT-6 Sol </div> </div> <figcaption><b>Figure 2:</b> Same task: hammer the nail. One model fixes its grasp after seeing the hammer tilt; the other doesn't. (3× speed)</figcaption> </figure> <h2 id="three-regimes">Three regimes</h2> <ul> <li><strong>R1 · Infer</strong> — predict a physical property from one observation.</li> <li><strong>R2 · Predict from experience</strong> — see earlier trials, then predict a new one.</li> <li><strong>R3 · Adapt</strong> — act, get feedback, try again until the goal is reached.</li> </ul> <div class="note"> <b>Oracle setting.</b> We can also hand the model ground-truth simulator values (mass, friction, …), step by step. This separates "didn't know the physics" from "couldn't use it". </div> <h2 id="the-benchmark">The benchmark</h2> <figure> <img src="/assets/img/blog/apro/dataset.png" alt="Example tasks"/> <figcaption><b>Figure 3:</b> Example tasks across the three regimes.</figcaption> </figure> <details class="setup"> <summary>Setup</summary> <ul> <li><b>Size:</b> 480 items, 11 tasks, 3 simulators (MuJoCo, Isaac Sim, OmniGibson).</li> <li><b>Models:</b> GPT-6 Sol, Gemini 4 Argon, Gemini 3.8 Flash, Claude Opus 5.5, Qwen3.5-27B, Qwen3.5-9B, DeepSeek-VL2.</li> <li><b>Robots (R3 tools):</b> Franka Panda + gripper, KUKA iiwa + Sharpa hand.</li> </ul> </details> <h2 id="r1-inferring-physical-properties">R1: Inferring physical properties</h2> <div class="exp-head"> <span class="exp-num">Finding 1</span> <h3>Evidence helps — when it's the right evidence</h3> </div> <p>One line about the result. (e.g. cup capacity jumps once the model is told the cup’s inner shape.)</p> <figure> <img src="/assets/img/blog/apro/r1_cup_capacity.png" alt="R1-1 cup capacity with evidence"/> <figcaption><b>Figure 4:</b> Cup capacity accuracy as evidence is added.</figcaption> </figure> <figure> <table class="results"> <thead> <tr><th>Model</th><th>Cup capacity</th><th>Material</th><th>Visible state</th><th>Fall block</th></tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr><td>GPT-6 Sol</td><td>40 → 82</td><td>50 → 74</td><td>54 → 46</td><td>70 → 84</td></tr> <tr><td>Gemini 4 Argon</td><td>48 → 72</td><td>56 → 70</td><td>52 → 50</td><td>54 → 72</td></tr> <tr><td>Claude Opus 5.5</td><td>50 → 84</td><td>58 → 70</td><td>60 → 52</td><td>56 → 80</td></tr> <tr><td>Qwen3.5-27B</td><td>24 → 62</td><td>28 → 54</td><td>50 → 54</td><td>58 → 50</td></tr> </tbody> </table> <figcaption><b>Table 1:</b> R1 accuracy (%), images only → all evidence.</figcaption> </figure> <h2 id="r2-predicting-from-experience">R2: Predicting from experience</h2> <div class="exp-head"> <span class="exp-num">Finding 2</span> <h3>The first two trials matter most</h3> </div> <p>One line about the result. More trials don’t always help; open-weight models can get worse.</p> <figure> <img src="/assets/img/blog/apro/r2_trials.png" alt="R2 accuracy vs number of prior trials"/> <figcaption><b>Figure 5:</b> Accuracy given <i>k</i> prior trials.</figcaption> </figure> <h2 id="r3-adapting-through-interaction">R3: Adapting through interaction</h2> <div class="exp-head"> <span class="exp-num">Experiment 3a</span> <h3>Can models discover hidden physics by trying?</h3> </div> <figure> <div class="vgrid"> <div class="cell"> <video src="/assets/video/blog/apro/seesaw_argon.mp4" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline=""></video> Balance the seesaw · Gemini 4 Argon (4×) </div> <div class="cell"> <video src="/assets/video/blog/apro/push_sol.mp4" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline=""></video> Push the box to the zone · GPT-6 Sol (3×) </div> </div> <figcaption><b>Figure 6:</b> Multi-trial rollouts. Each trial reveals something about mass or friction.</figcaption> </figure> <figure> <img src="/assets/img/blog/apro/r3_successrate.png" alt="Success within k trials"/> <figcaption><b>Figure 7:</b> Success within <i>k</i> trials. Stars: with oracle evidence.</figcaption> </figure> <p>One line about the result. (e.g. Argon is too gentle on push; evidence fixes it.)</p> <div class="exp-head"> <span class="exp-num">Experiment 3b</span> <h3>Can models use tools?</h3> </div> <figure> <div class="vgrid four"> <div class="cell"><video src="/assets/video/blog/apro/skills_argon_sweep.mp4" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline=""></video>Sweep <span class="tag-ok">✓</span></div> <div class="cell"><video src="/assets/video/blog/apro/skills_argon_pan.mp4" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline=""></video>Pan <span class="tag-ok">✓</span></div> <div class="cell"><video src="/assets/video/blog/apro/skills_argon_stir.mp4" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline=""></video>Stir <span class="tag-ok">✓</span></div> <div class="cell"><video src="/assets/video/blog/apro/skills_argon_flip.mp4" autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline=""></video>Flip <span class="tag-fail">✗</span></div> </div> <figcaption><b>Figure 8:</b> Gemini 4 Argon with high-level skills on the Sharpa hand. (3×)</figcaption> </figure> <figure> <table class="results"> <thead> <tr><th>Robot / interface</th><th>Argon</th><th>Sol</th><th>Opus 5.5</th><th>Qwen-27B</th><th>Qwen-9B</th></tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr><td>Sharpa · joints</td><td><b>6/10</b></td><td>0/10</td><td>4/10</td><td>0/10</td><td>0/10</td></tr> <tr><td>Sharpa · skills</td><td><b>8/10</b></td><td>6/10</td><td><b>8/10</b></td><td>1/10</td><td>0/10</td></tr> <tr><td>Franka · joints</td><td>5/10</td><td>4/10</td><td><b>6/10</b></td><td>0/10</td><td>0/10</td></tr> </tbody> </table> <figcaption><b>Table 2:</b> Tool tasks completed out of 10.</figcaption> </figure> <p>One line about the result. (e.g. skills ≫ joints → low-level control is the bottleneck.)</p> <figure> <img src="/assets/img/blog/apro/qualitative.png" alt="Qualitative tool rollouts"/> <figcaption><b>Figure 9:</b> Success vs. failure, frame by frame.</figcaption> </figure> <h2 id="takeaways">Takeaways</h2> <ol> <li>Models can infer physics, but struggle to <strong>act</strong> on it.</li> <li>Past trials help most at the <strong>start</strong>.</li> <li>Giving the true physics helps prediction, but <strong>not always manipulation</strong> — execution is the bottleneck.</li> </ol> <div class="note"> <b>Limitations.</b> Simulation only; few tool tasks; no human baseline. </div> <h2 id="citation">Citation</h2> <pre class="bibtex"><code>@article{apro2026,
  title   = {Measuring Agentic Physical Reasoning},
  author  = {Lee, Heekyung and Wang, Zirui and Ryan, Fiona and Chan, David M. and Darrell, Trevor and Bai, Yutong},
  journal = {arXiv preprint},
  year    = {2026}
}</code></pre>]]></content><author><name>Heekyung Lee</name></author><category term="research"/><category term="robotics"/><category term="vlm"/><category term="benchmark"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Can VLMs turn what they see about physics into actions that work?]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Example Post</title><link href="https://kyunnilee.github.io/blog/2025/advanced-images/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Example Post"/><published>2025-06-10T22:08:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-06-10T22:08:00+00:00</updated><id>https://kyunnilee.github.io/blog/2025/advanced-images</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://kyunnilee.github.io/blog/2025/advanced-images/"><![CDATA[<p>Blog section is still in construction.</p> <h2 id="example-image-slider">Example image slider</h2> <p>Some random Images.</p> <swiper-container keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/9-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/9-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/9-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/9.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/7-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/7-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/7-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/7.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/8-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/8-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/8-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" 